      "title": "Letterboxd review of Horrible Bosses",
      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"Horrible Bosses\"] Look this movie was funny. I laughed a good few times. Jason Bateman, Charlie Day and Jason Sudeikis were all great and had good chemistry and hit all the comedic beats really well.But there’s a recurring plot line in this where Charlie Day is repeatedly sexually harassed by his boss (and even full-on raped by her!!!), and it’s played off by everyone as “Ahhh it’s not a big deal though cos she’s hot.” It’s supposed to be funny cos he’s a man and most men would enjoy sex with Jennifer Aniston. Like, nah, treat rape with the appropriate seriousness please and don’t just play it for jokes because",
